message: "If you use this benchmark, protocol, or executable reference substrate in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "Validation and Evaluation Protocol (VEP) for Agent Execution Governance and Post-Compromise Containment"
authors:
  - family-names: "Chen"
    given-names: "Chun-Cheng"
    alias: "Jimmy Chen"
    affiliation: "Top-Celestial Company Ltd."
version: 0.2.1
date-released: 2026-09-02
url: "https://github.com/top-celestial-company-ltd/dros-vep-lite"
keywords:
  - "agent execution governance"
  - "agent execution authority"
  - "post-compromise agent security"
  - "post-compromise execution containment"
  - "deterministic runtime enforcement"
  - "agent authorization"
  - "runtime security"
  - "agent security benchmark"
  - "execution control plane"
  - "reproducible security evaluation"
  - "fail-closed execution"
  - "executable research substrate"
abstract: >-
  VEP is an open, implementation-independent evaluation protocol designed to measure
  whether AI agent execution security controls remain deterministically effective
  after compromise. DROS provides one executable reference substrate for VEP-based evaluation.
